00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.420
If you’re finding me for the first time,
all you have to do to participate is be a

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.540
subscriber and leave a comment on those videos.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:38.710
And be nice to everyone.

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:40.070
So let’s answers some questions.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:43.060
Careful for spoilers from the episode if you’re
not caught up.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:49.190
Also during question five I talk a lot about
Jon Snow’s supposed parents, even though

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:50.950
the books haven’t said who they are, everyone
has their theories.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.899
So if you want to avoid that, just watch for
the spoiler warning and then skip ahead in

00:00:54.899 --> 00:00:55.899
the video.

00:00:55.899 --> 00:00:57.410
Here we go.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:02.150
Question 1 - Cleetus Van Damme asks Are there
any references to the Thenns being cannibals

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:03.150
in the books?﻿

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:11.261
I believe that the Skagos tribes were the
cannibals in the books, but because they didn’t

00:01:11.261 --> 00:01:13.890
want to have to cast more people they just
gave that trait to the Thenns.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:17.320
Remember when Jon Snow was telling the Night’s
Watch council about the Wildling Army.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:22.530
It’s a hundred thousand strong, so there’s
no way they can portray all those people.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:31.409
If we do get to see them this season, they’ll
probably do a lot of CG crowd duplication.

00:01:31.409 --> 00:01:35.920
Question 2 - Ray Ray asks Based on this episode,
how well do you think that they will stick

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.070
to the book?﻿

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:44.360
DB Weiss and David Benioff are really committed
to honoring the original text, so all the

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.130
major sign posts will be there.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:51.220
And for anyone who’s read the books, all
the biggest stuff will always be there.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:54.670
It’s just the smaller things that they have
to combine or omit all together.

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:56.310
Like the Ser Dontos scene.

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:59.670
In the books it was a hairnet but on the show
it was a necklace.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:03.940
That’s a minor change, with Arya and the
Hound who knows.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:08.000
In one of the trailers we saw her in the middle
of a training montage with Needle.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.810
That’s probably from the first couple of
episodes.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:14.379
I don’t think they’ll totally change her
story from the books, but there are always

00:02:14.379 --> 00:02:16.500
the Shae exceptions.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:21.069
When I say that, I mean they can choose to
keep characters they feel work really well

00:02:21.069 --> 00:02:27.650
together, in more scenes than they had in
the books.

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:32.440
So thus we could see more Hound and Arya palling
their way to the Vale than was in the books.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:36.939
Question 3 - Vegtabadass asks if the dragons
keep growing, could they get as big as Smaug

00:02:36.939 --> 00:02:38.239
from The Hobbit?

00:02:38.239 --> 00:02:43.450
I saw a fictional dragon size chart that listed
Smaug as the biggest fictional dragon ever

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.450
created.

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:46.469
Like as big as an apartment complex.

00:02:46.469 --> 00:02:50.500
The biggest dragon in the history of Westeros
was Balerion the Black Dread.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.060
Aegon the Conqueror's dragon.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:56.390
There are a lot of things about Daenerys and
her three dragons that mirrors Aegon, his

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.360
two sisters and their three dragons.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.749
For instance, their three dragons were the
same colors as Daenerys.

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:06.680
So I think George RR Martin is implying that
Drogon will be just like Balerion.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.249
He’s still very young.

00:03:08.249 --> 00:03:10.620
Balerion lived to about two hundred years
old.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.670
But remember, he had no natural predators.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:16.160
When Aegon first brought them to Westeros,
they were essentially unchallenged.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:21.550
I think now there are more people like Tyrion
and other Maesters who are educated on dragonlore.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:25.739
Their size is just a function of food supply
and age.

00:03:25.739 --> 00:03:28.469
So the longer the live and the more they eat,
the more they grow.

00:03:28.469 --> 00:03:32.829
Question 4 - Stephen Herman asks Do you like
how they changed Arya and The Hound from the

00:03:32.829 --> 00:03:33.999
book?

00:03:33.999 --> 00:03:36.220
I do like it, The Hound and Arya are one of
the best pairs on the show.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:42.499
It’s hard to tell if they’ll stay completely
faithful to the books, but until we see otherwise

00:03:42.499 --> 00:03:45.519
let’s just assume that the biggest events
will still happen the way they’re supposed

00:03:45.519 --> 00:03:46.519
too.

00:03:46.519 --> 00:03:49.750
I guess if they ended up doing something radically
different from the books it wouldn’t be

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:50.750
terrible.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.420
The writing is great and the actors are amazing.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:54.250
So no matter what I’ll keep watching.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:57.050
I don’t get upset when they drop characters
or eliminate things.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:58.829
Careful for spoilers in this one.

00:03:58.829 --> 00:04:02.459
I basically try to connect the dots on who
Jon Snow’s mother is, so if you don’t

00:04:02.459 --> 00:04:03.989
want to know.

00:04:03.989 --> 00:04:07.959
Just skip ahead in the video about 30 seconds.

00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:12.109
Question 5 - All The World’s A Stage actually
pointed something out that I wanted to include.

00:04:12.109 --> 00:04:15.549
When you freeze frame on the White Book page
for Gerold Hightower it tells some more of

00:04:15.549 --> 00:04:16.549
the backstory of what happened to Lyanna Stark.

00:04:16.549 --> 00:04:18.800
Hightower was the commander of the Kingsguard
before Barristan Selmy.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:23.850
He was in charge when Jaime murdered King
Aerys during Robert’s rebellion.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:28.091
Before he died, King Aerys sent Hightower
and a couple of men to find Rhaegar when he

00:04:28.091 --> 00:04:29.600
ran off with Lyanna Stark.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.970
He found the two at the Tower of Joy which
was in the North part of Dorne.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:41.270
Rhaegar left and made Hightower stay behind
to guard Lyanna, eventually Eddard Stark found

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:43.889
them and ended up killing Hightower and his
men.

00:04:43.889 --> 00:04:47.560
When they found Lyanna she was lying in a
bed of blood.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:55.030
This is where all the Jon Snow theories come
from.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:59.640
The implication is that when Hightower found
Rhaegar and Lyanna, she was pregnant, so Rhaegar

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:01.440
asked Hightower to stay and guard her.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.510
She died as a result of the childbirth and
Eddard Stark got there just as Jon Snow was

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:06.510
being born.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:11.030
He took him and to protect him, named him
his own bastard.

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:13.460
Thus he’s a Son of Ice and Fire.

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:16.470
So that’s what that page in the White Book
is all about.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:21.800
Oberyn Martell’s comments corroborate some
of the theory.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:26.860
Question 6 - No Sherlock asks Are we going
to see any other Martell’s this season?

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:30.930
There isn’t a lot of Dorne as a geographical
location in Book 3, so I don’t think we’ll

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.380
see it a lot or the other Martells until season
5.

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:36.940
Think of it in terms of Daenerys journey to
different cities in the east.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.040
Each season she goes to more and more places.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.860
So eventually we’ll see plenty of Dorne.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:44.060
It’s really different from the rest of Westeros
so I can’t wait.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:49.500
There’s a lot of really cool characters
they can potentially introduce.

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:53.280
Question 7 - Hyrule Savior Asks Is Oberon
Daenerys’ Uncle?﻿

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:58.800
No, Daenerys is the youngest child of King
Aerys, her mother was also a Targaryen.

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:01.030
Remember all the sister wiving they did.

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:03.610
She’s first cousins with the Martells.

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:06.530
Prince Doran’s sister was Elia, who married
Rhaegar.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:09.270
Oberyn is Doran’s younger brother.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:14.340
Question 8 - Jesse Wade asks Do you feel that
Arya is maturing as a character in much the

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.880
same way that Carl is in TWD?﻿

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:20.290
Yes, but their characters are headed in opposite
directions.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:22.820
They’re both at a crossroads so to speak.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:26.350
Appropriate since, Arya was just literally
at the crossroads.

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:29.920
Carl is trying to decide whether or not he’s
becoming a monster and he doesn’t want to

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:32.120
be, he’s trying to stay a good person.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.180
Arya on the other hand is embracing the dark
path she’s on.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:38.130
She’s slowly turning into a killer and is
really enjoying the thought of that.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.740
For her it means revenge.

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:47.060
Question 9 - Dex asks Which character’s
story are you most excited to see this season?

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:51.430
In no particular order, Tyrion Lannister,
Jon Snow, Bran Stark and Arya.

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:57.590
Without going further, I feel like there are
so many interesting things happening this

00:06:57.590 --> 00:07:00.409
season it’s hard to pin down just one character.

00:07:00.409 --> 00:07:05.270
Question 10 - Pseudo Nym asks Episode 2 the
Rose and the Lion sounds like the Purple Wedding,

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:06.590
is that true?

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:12.600
Yes, from trailer for next week it looks like
we’ll see all the wedding scenes.

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:17.770
They said it was the biggest shoot since the
season 1 premiere in terms of number of people

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.140
on set those days.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:24.060
Charles Dance said the wedding and the banquet
after felt like a short film all by itself

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:25.060
just because it was so elaborate.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:30.981
and one last Bonus Question - Silver blaze
mist asks How about the Ser Duncan the Tall

00:07:30.981 --> 00:07:31.981
Shout out?

00:07:31.981 --> 00:07:33.890
Yes, also from the White Book.

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:38.150
When Joffrey is flipping through it he talks
about Ser Duncan the tall.

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:42.760
From the Dunk and Egg spinoff books that George
RR Martin wrote.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:47.170
You should read them if you haven’t I talk
about them a bunch in the Game of Thrones

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:49.170
Movie video I did a while ago.

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:51.670
I’ll add a link to that at the end of this
video.

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:55.030
But thanks so much for submitting questions.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:56.800
This season is going to be so much fun.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:01.840
It’s going to be hard to talk about everything
without going crazy on spoilers, so I’ll

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:10.100
